00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:27.030
Here we define what we mean by
cybersecurity threat hunting.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:31.380
Different teams define threat
huntings in different ways,

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:34.920
but the most common and
useful definition is this.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:39.660
You are proactively searching
through your environment

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.840
for a threat or a
set of activities

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.770
that you have not
previously detected.

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:51.240
That phrase not previously
detected is the key point.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:56.100
This is what separates threat
hunting from incident response

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.290
or alert triage which starts

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.410
from something that's
already been flagged.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.740
Threat hunting is
meant to be continual.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.660
You ask good questions.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.490
You search for evidence.

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:10.770
You learn from what you find.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.810
And you repeat the cycle

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:17.220
to steadily reduce
attacker (inaudible) time.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.880
Now let's talk about building
a threat hunting hypothesis

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.170
because good hunting starts
with a good hypothesis.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:27.420
First keep it achievable.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:30.720
If it's too ambitious
it won't get finished.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:36.720
Second keep the scope narrow so
you can validate or disprove it

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.840
with the data you have.

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.850
Third keep it time bound.

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:46.640
Define a clear window like the
last 24 hours, the last 7 days,

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.240
or a specific time
frame around an event.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.240
Fourth keep it
useful and efficient

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:59.940
so the work produces actionable
insights rather than just noise.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.200
And fifth keep it related to the
threat model you're defending

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:09.480
against so your hunting effort
is aligned to the adversaries

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:15.060
and techniques that matter
most to your organization.

